# Long-term CO₂ exchange at US-Brw (Utqiaġvik, Alaska), 2002–2024

R code and data to reproduce the temporal trend analyses, Table 1, Fig. 2 and
Fig. S5 of Oechel et al., in review.

## Files

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `TOT_MET_FLX_v2026_11_13_f.csv` | Annual values of monthly NEE and environmental variables, 2000–2024 (NA = no data) |
| `R_script_Fig.2_trend_analysis_US-Brw.R` | Trend analyses, tables and figures |

### Data columns

| Column(s) | Description | Units |
|---|---|---|
| `Year` | Year | – |
| `NEE_May` … `NEE_Oct` | Monthly cumulative net ecosystem exchange (negative = uptake) | g C-CO₂ m⁻² month⁻¹ |
| `SoilT_May` … `SoilT_Oct` | Monthly mean soil temperature | °C |
| `SWC_May` … `SWC_Oct`, `SWC_JJA_median` | Monthly mean soil water content | % |
| `GDD_June` … `GDD_Sept`, `GDD_JJA` | Growing degree days | °C d |
| `melt_date_NOAA`, `Snow_In_NOAA`, `Snow_free_NOAA`, `Snow Season Length_NOAA` | Snowmelt date, snow onset date, snow-free days, snow season length (NOAA) | day of year / days |
| `U1_Barrow_mean` | Mean active-layer (thaw) depth | cm |

## Requirements

R (≥ 4.0) and the packages `zyp`, `nlme` and `mgcv`:

```r
install.packages(c("zyp", "nlme", "mgcv"))
```

## How to run

1. Download this repository and keep the script and the CSV file in the same folder.
2. Open R or RStudio and set the working directory to that folder:
   ```r
   setwd("path/to/this/folder")
   ```
3. Run the script:
   ```r
   source("R_script_Fig.2_trend_analysis_US-Brw.R")
   ```

All outputs are written to the same folder.

## Outputs

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `Table_1_trends.csv` | Trend statistics for all NEE months and environmental variables (Table 1) |
| `Table_NEE_trends.csv` | NEE and driver trends and NEE–driver correlations for the Fig. 2 panels |
| `Fig_2.tiff`, `Fig_2.pdf` | Fig. 2 (600 dpi TIFF) |
| `FigS5_ACF_OLS_residuals.tiff`, `.pdf`, `.csv` | Fig. S5: autocorrelation of OLS residuals, and the values plotted |

## Methods summary

Temporal trends were tested with OLS regression, Kendall's rank correlation test,
the Yue–Pilon pre-whitened Mann–Kendall test (`zyp`) and GLS regression with
continuous-time AR(1) errors (`nlme`). Non-linear change was tested with GAMs
(`mgcv`; k = 6, REML), and is reported where edf > 1.5, ΔAIC > 2 relative to a
linear model, and p < 0.05. Years without data are retained as gaps.
Significance threshold: p < 0.05.

